  "description": "EGEYIZ crystallizes in the monoclinic crystal system with space group C 2/c. Reported CIF formula moiety: C96 H134 N52 O58 Pr6 8+,11(Br1 1-),3(H3 O1 1+),26(H2 O1). From the CIF bond table, Pr1 (Pr) has 9 O neighbors; Pr2 (Pr) has 9 O neighbors; Pr3 (Pr) has 9 O neighbors; Pr1B (Pr) has 9 O neighbors; Pr2B (Pr) has 9 O neighbors; Pr3B (Pr) has 9 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 6 pairs, 3 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.780-3.977 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 88.57-110.18°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula (H3O)3{[Pr4(OH)8(H2O)4(IN@CB[6])2][Pr(H2O)7(HIN)]2}Br11·26H2O. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 8 OH (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 4 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 7 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article formula).",
